    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1074">

                <pb facs="0836" n="754" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg754"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 831.415 A/11.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic">June 12,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President has decided to send a special ambassador, accompanied by a
                    secretary and military and naval attaches, to the centenary of Venezuelan
                    independence. Mr. Thomas C. Dawson is named special ambassador and Capt. Marsh,
                    United States Navy, commanding the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">North
                        Carolina</hi>, will be naval attaché to the special mission. The above named
                    vessel will carry the mission to La Guaira, Venezuela. The names of the
                    secretary and military attaché to the mission will be sent later.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
